      "writtenOn": "2026-03-17T17:30:14Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "The previous logic that made the last worker be the one to re-use the \"common\" buffers seems needlessly complicated, because the number of workers can increase or decrease, and so will the `worker_idx` of the last worker.\n\nIt makes more sense to have the first worker (`worker_idx \u003d 0`) reuse the \"common\" buffers instead, so its position never changes no matter how many workers there are at a time.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 625,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 637,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "288ad69242232a60dac6dca5697cb0154a7f39dc",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4483f331_5d706167",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/ethread.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 844,
      "author": {
        "id": 3678645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-17T17:41:19Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "This function didn\u0027t really \"initialize\" anything. Its only purpose was to make the last \"visible\" worker have the restoration buffers assigned from `AV1_COMMON` if the total number of workers changed. However, the references for the buffers that were previously dynamically generated are completely lost (and so they can no longer be free\u0027d), causing a resource lifetime issue.\n\nMaking the first worker always reuse the buffers from `AV1_COMMON` obviates doing the reassignment that this function did.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 830,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 844,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "288ad69242232a60dac6dca5697cb0154a7f39dc",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
