      "writtenOn": "2026-03-17T17:14:26Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "The shortcut this function uses (`subpel_x_q3 | subpel_y_q3`) to conditionally upsample the prediction buffer with `aom_upsampled_pred()` is particularly strange (premature optimization?), and breaks frame scaling.\n\nOther functions like `aom_highbd_comp_mask_upsampled_pred()` or `aom_highbd_comp_avg_upsampled_pred_[c|neon|sse2]()` unconditionally call `aom_upsampled_pred()`, so this change follows the same pattern for this function as well.\n\n`aom_upsampled_pred()` itself optimizes for the \"no subpel, no scaling\" special case, so it\u0027d be most correct for the function to handle the case.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 526,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 533,
        "endChar": 75
      },
      "revId": "288ad69242232a60dac6dca5697cb0154a7f39dc",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
