      "side": 0,
      "message": "\u003e The shortcut this function uses (`subpel_x_q3 | subpel_y_q3`) to conditionally upsample the prediction buffer with `aom_upsampled_pred()` is particularly strange (premature optimization?), and breaks frame scaling.\n\u003e \n\u003e Other functions like `aom_highbd_comp_mask_upsampled_pred()` or `aom_highbd_comp_avg_upsampled_pred_[c|neon|sse2]()` unconditionally call `aom_upsampled_pred()`, so this change follows the same pattern for this function as well.\n\u003e \n\u003e `aom_upsampled_pred()` itself optimizes for the \"no subpel, no scaling\" special case, so it\u0027d be most correct for the function to handle the case.\n\nIt looks like that behavior came from https://aomedia-review.git.corp.google.com/c/aom/+/44241.",
